 the outer 1‑frame becomes 1. That includes the 2‑frame, the 8‑block and the 3‑block.\n\nThe fact sheet's colour transitions agree exactly. Every change is \"inner colour → colour of the outermost enclosing frame\", for example 4→2, 1→2, 6→1, 1→7, 2/3/4→8.\n\n**Rule.** For every object, look for objects whose bounding box strictly contains its bounding box. If there are any, recolour the object to the colour of the outermost one (the one with the largest bounding box). Objects that nothing encloses keep their colour.\n\n**Construction stages.** I handle one top‑level frame at a time and emit after each. Each stage recolours everything nested inside that one frame.\n\n**On the test input.**\n- The 4‑frame at the top contains a 3‑frame, an 8‑frame and a 1‑block, so all of them become 4.\n- The 1‑frame at the bottom left contains a 3‑frame and a 2‑block, so they become 1.\n- The 8‑frame at the bottom right contains a 4‑ring, which becomes 8.\n- The lone 6‑bar is not enclosed by anything, so it stays 6.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n\n    def inside(a, b):  # a's box strictly inside b's box\n        ay0, ax0, ay1, ax1 = a[\"box\"]\n        by0, bx0, by1, bx1 = b[\"box\"]\n        return by0 < ay0 and bx0 < ax0 and ay1 < by1 and ax1 < bx1\n\n    def area(o):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        return (y1 - y0 + 1) * (x1 - x0 + 1)\n\n    # assign each enclosed object to its outermost enclosing object\n    groups = {}\n    for i, o in enumerate(objs):\n        encl = [j for j, p in enumerate(objs) if j != i and inside(o, p)]\n        if encl:\n            top = max(encl, key=lambda j: area(objs[j]))\n            groups.setdefault(top, []).append(i)\n\n    out = g.copy()\n    for top in sorted(groups):\n        col = objs[top][\"colour\"]\n        for i in groups[top]:\n            for (y, x) in objs[i][\"cells\"]:\n                out[y, x] = col\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Recolour everything nested inside the colour-{col} frame to {col}.\")\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final grid: all nested shapes take the colour of their outermost frame.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"If there are any, recolour the object to the colour of the outermost one (the one with the largest bounding box)."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"If there are any, recolour the object to the colour of the outermost one (the one with the largest bounding box)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each stage recolours everything nested inside that one frame."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Recolour everything nested inside the colour-1 frame to 1."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The 3‑frame encloses nothing and contains nothing, so it stays 3."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Every change is \"inner colour → colour of the outermost enclosing frame\", for example 4→2, 1→2, 6→1, 1→7, 2/3/4→8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Objects that nothing encloses keep their colour."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Rule.** For every object, look for objects whose bounding box strictly contains its bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"If there are any, recolour the object to the colour of the outermost one (the one with the largest bounding box)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"871e113eab1513f8ae093c53066633d31ba738bd5688107d12e7e04cf0f6ded7","task_sha256":"6bc92afa4172fc3c01e86bd42aef9a0e8de20dfe0d37bbda792571013587ba56","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
